Prehľad o zrazených a odvedených preddavkoch na daň (PREHLAD_2026). FS SR keeps one XSD per vzor and keeps the old ones, so a new vintage
arrives as a NEW file name rather than as a change to this one. The probes
made on 2026-10-27 for a newer vintage or a _v2 revision beside this name all
returned 404.

THE FILE CANNOT PROVE IT IS CURRENT. Its annotation stamps a vintage at most,
not a revision, and nothing validates the annotation; a file revised in place
validates exactly as before. That is why the digest is pinned here.

REFRESH PROCEDURE
  1. Fetch the name above and compare md5 and size with the line here.
  2. Check the STATUS CODE, not the size: a miss returns 404 with a
     ~1 245-byte HTML error page, which is a perfectly plausible file size.
  3. Probe for a newer vintage as well as a _v2 suffix on the existing name —
     FS SR published a DPPO revision as dppo2025_v2.xsd beside an unchanged
     dppo2025.xsd, and a digest comparison on a pinned name cannot see that.
  4. A new vintage is a new cssk.payroll.declaration.version record with its
     own template; update this file and re-run the module's tests.
